{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of Jaeger's 4-flow theorem: every finite 4-edge-connected simple graph has a nowhere-zero integer 4-flow, i.e. an antisymmetric function on darts with values in {±1, ±2, ±3} that is conserved at every vertex. Also proved: a graph with two edge-disjoint spanning trees has its edges covered by two even subgraphs (a nowhere-zero ℤ₂ × ℤ₂-flow) and has a nowhere-zero integer 4-flow. Mathlib has no flows. Jaeger's 8-flow theorem for bridgeless graphs is not included.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Juan Pablo Traverso Gianini"
    }
  ],
